$DIR/test.p:7:1: missing return
    f is declared on line 2 to return int, but the end of its body on line 7 can
    be reached without a return statement. Every path through a function with
    results must end in a return, a panic, or a loop that never exits.
    Return a value at the end, for example:
        return 0
    (see "Terminating statements" in the Plutonium spec, section 12.1)
    (run "pluto explain E0102" for a longer explanation)
